@page "/about"
@layout MarketingLayout

<PageTitle>About | My Active Vitals</PageTitle>

<header class="marketing-page-hero">
    <p class="marketing-kicker">About My Active Vitals</p>
    <h1>Health data should feel understandable—not scattered.</h1>
    <p>My Active Vitals was created to make personal health tracking more connected, practical, and useful in everyday life.</p>
</header>

<section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="marketing-copy">
            <h2>Why we are building it</h2>
            <p>Important details often end up spread across paper notes, device apps, patient portals, and memory. My Active Vitals brings the information you choose to track into one personal record.</p>
            <p>The goal is not to replace clinicians or medical systems. It is to help you arrive at daily decisions and healthcare conversations with clearer context.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="marketing-feature-panel">
            <strong>Our product principles</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>Make daily entry straightforward</li>
                <li>Show trends without overwhelming people</li>
                <li>Treat health information with care</li>
                <li>Be clear about what the product can and cannot do</li>
                <li>Keep medical decisions between people and qualified professionals</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="marketing-section marketing-section--tint">
    <div class="marketing-section__heading">
        <p class="marketing-kicker">Who it helps</p>
        <h2>Built for people managing the details.</h2>
        <p>My Active Vitals is designed for adults who want a consistent view of nutrition, exercise, vital readings, weight, fluids, and kidney health information.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="marketing-card-grid">
        <article class="marketing-card">
            <h3>Daily trackers</h3>
            <p>For people replacing notebooks and disconnected spreadsheets with one organized history.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="marketing-card">
            <h3>Trend watchers</h3>
            <p>For people who want to see how readings and routines change over days, weeks, and months.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="marketing-card">
            <h3>Kidney-conscious users</h3>
            <p>For people paying closer attention to fluids and nutrients such as sodium, potassium, and phosphorus.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="marketing-cta">
    <h2>See what My Active Vitals can track.</h2>
    <p>Explore the tools that connect daily entries with a longer-term view.</p>
    <a class="marketing-button" href="features">Explore features</a>
</section>
